<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Burgundians</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Burgundians were an East Germanic people who crossed the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rhine">Rhine</a> in the early 5th century and founded a kingdom as Roman allies around 411, traditionally centred on Worms. After its destruction by Hunnic troops in Roman service in 436, the survivors were settled in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sapaudia">Sapaudia</a> around <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/geneva">Geneva</a> in 443, where they built a new kingdom in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rhone">Rhône</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saone">Saône</a> valleys. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/frankish-kingdom">Franks</a> conquered it in 534, and its name lives on in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/burgundy">Burgundy</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/burgundians.jpg" alt="Burgundians" width="320" height="283" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Altaileopard · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Conquests_of_Clovis.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
